 <section class="three-tool-section" id="chart-deep-meaning"><h3>What is a Salah checklist and is tracking worship obligatory?</h3><p>A checklist is a voluntary planning method. Islam prescribes Salah at appointed times, but no source makes using a printed tracking sheet an obligation. <a href="https://quran.com/4/103">Quran 4:103</a> establishes the importance of prayer times; using a tickbox is a modern organisational preference rather than a prescribed ritual. The paper is not a measure of sincerity, acceptance or religious standing.</p></section>
 <section class="three-tool-section" id="chart-deep-create"><h3>How to print a prayer checklist step by step</h3><ol><li>Pick the first civil date for the chart.</li><li>Select a 7-day, 14-day or 30-day schedule.</li><li>Optionally write a heading such as 'My Salah chart'.</li><li>Check the preview, which lists Fajr, Dhuhr, Asr, Maghrib and Isha for every date.</li><li>Choose Print / Save PDF in your browser; scale or switch paper orientation if needed.</li><li>Mark your own chart privately after prayer, or download an entirely blank CSV for editing.</li></ol></section>
 <section class="three-tool-section" id="chart-deep-five"><h3>The five Fard prayers and what each column represents</h3><p>The five daily obligatory prayers are Fajr, Dhuhr, Asr, Maghrib and Isha. Sunrise is not an additional Fard prayer, and Witr/Sunnah prayers have distinct rulings. The checkboxes refer to your own acknowledgement of a prayer, not an automatic determination that it was prayed correctly or on time. Refer to the <a href="/tools/prayer-rakats-chart/">Rakats chart</a> for Fard units.</p></section>
 <section class="three-tool-section" id="chart-deep-calendar"><h3>What if I cross a month boundary or travel?</h3><p>The generator advances Gregorian dates at UTC noon to avoid daylight-saving day-skips in the printed date list. It does not assert that a prayer's religious day begins or ends at civil midnight. When travelling or changing timezones, use a reliable <a href="/tools/prayer-times/">prayer time calculation</a> or a qualified local mosque timetable rather than inferring prayer windows from the paper date.</p></section>
 <section class="three-tool-section" id="chart-deep-example"><h3>Worked example: a 14-day printable prayer chart</h3><div class="three-tool-example"><p>Choose 1 November 2026 and 14 days. The generator prints rows for 1–14 November and five blank prayer squares per row: <strong>14 × 5 = 70 blank boxes</strong>. There is no evidence of 70 missed prayers; the boxes are blank until someone chooses to record them.</p><p>The same 14-day table can be printed as a one-page or multi-page PDF depending on browser scaling and paper size. The CSV provides the underlying date-and-prayer columns without personal marks.</p></div></section>
 <section class="three-tool-section" id="chart-deep-privacy"><h3>Is the chart private and does the site save it?</h3><p>The form generates a blank document in your current browser. It does not upload your prayer record or save names, marks or dates to an account. After printing or downloading, responsibility for protecting a marked paper or file rests with whoever stores it. An empty box is unknown, not a ruling that the prayer needs Qada.</p></section>
 <section class="three-tool-section" id="chart-deep-families"><h3>Using a chart with children or family members</h3><p>Parents can encourage learning through gentle, age-appropriate routines, but the responsibility and applicability of Salah differs by age and circumstance. Avoid turning tracking into public comparison or shame. Younger children may learn prayer names and sequence without implying that every unticked square means a religious failure.</p></section>
 <section class="three-tool-section" id="chart-deep-mistakes"><h3>Common mistakes with printable prayer charts</h3><p>Do not confuse Fard, Sunnah and Witr into one obligatory category, mark an unrecorded date as 'missed', infer prayer correctness from a tick, or assume Gregorian date lines are a verified local mosque timetable. Use the <a href="/tools/salah-tracker/">digital tracker</a> for voluntary private logging and the <a href="/tools/qada-prayer-calculator/">Qada planning tool</a> only after checking which prayers are actually owed.</p></section>
